# Files that get sourced or executed as shell scripts must always check
# out with LF line endings, on every platform - a CRLF PKGBUILD makes
# makepkg/bash refuse to source it at all ("contains CRLF characters and
# cannot be sourced"), which is exactly what broke the Windows CI package
# job despite the repo's own blobs being LF-only: GitHub's windows-latest
# runners default to git core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF -> CRLF on
# checkout unless overridden here.
packaging/msys2/**/PKGBUILD text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
